  - route: TapTraining
    root: {fileID: 1590525177}
    title: {fileID: 328110931}
    brief: {fileID: 1343468476}
  - route: Skills
    root: {fileID: 216725752}
    title: {fileID: 1715781931}
    brief: {fileID: 332345706}
  - route: SkillDetail
    root: {fileID: 600262865}
    title: {fileID: 1658930171}
    brief: {fileID: 1600376966}
  - route: DrawReveal
    root: {fileID: 297627011}
    title: {fileID: 1830005996}
    brief: {fileID: 2036377159}
  - route: Upgrades
    root: {fileID: 802250564}
    title: {fileID: 1335225015}
    brief: {fileID: 1185202205}
  - route: Prestige
    root: {fileID: 798145335}
    title: {fileID: 1182889096}
    brief: {fileID: 1863376222}
  - route: Offline
    root: {fileID: 861227123}
    title: {fileID: 205525028}
    brief: {fileID: 45593532}
  - route: BuyAll
    root: {fileID: 1087925743}
    title: {fileID: 1610811750}
    brief: {fileID: 1055113994}
  topics:
  - id: buy-first
    title: Your first purchase
    brief: Buy one Phuljhari yourself.
    body: Open Products and buy one Phuljhari with your opening cash. No product
      is bought automatically. Its sales then earn cash for this run; the opening
      grant itself does not count toward Prestige.
  - id: tap-counter
    title: A useful tap
    brief: Only the counter earns tap cash.
    body: Tap the stall counter to earn cash. Up to three full-value taps count per
      second. Scrolling or using menus never earns a tap.
  - id: product-levels
    title: Choose your quantity
    brief: Review x1, x10, x100 or Max.
    body: Product levels raise normal sales. Choose x1, x10, x100 or Max, then review
      the exact count and cost before buying. Tap training has its own level quote.
  - id: catalogue-filters
    title: Find the next upgrade
    brief: The next ten are ready in Player.
    body: Player shows the next ten eligible cash upgrades. Each row states its effect
      and price. Buy directly, or open the catalogue to search and filter. These
      upgrades need only cash and their listed run requirements, never Fame or completed
      prestiges.
  - id: buy-all
    title: Buy affordable upgrades
    brief: Buy All spends cash on eligible upgrades.
    body: Player's Buy All immediately buys affordable eligible cash upgrades in
      price order. In the catalogue, Review Buy All shows the scoped list before
      purchase. Neither buys product levels or Talent, nor spends KK.
  - id: skill-basics
    title: Skills for this run
    brief: Buy the base skill, then activate it.
    body: Base skills must be bought again each run. Activate a ready skill; its
      cooldown starts immediately. Reading menus does not pause sales or skill timers.
  - id: comebacks
    title: An earlier shelf can grow
    brief: Compare its normal income and share.
    body: Signature cash upgrades improve earlier products and change their display
      at signatures I, IV and X. These appearances rebuild each run. Shop decorations
      earned from lifetime discoveries stay after Prestige.
  - id: prestige
    title: Know what stays
    brief: Fame, cards and shop progress stay.
    body: Run earnings fill the Prestige target. Reset rebuilds products and cash
      upgrades. Fame, Talent, unique purchases and decorations stay. First Prestige
      grants three free draws.
  - id: rebuild
    title: A new run, familiar shop
    brief: Buy the first product manually again.
    body: Your opening cash is ready for a manual first purchase. Fame and cards
      improve this rebuild. Product displays and skills return only after you buy
      their run requirements.
  - id: cash-and-talent
    title: Two kinds of upgrades
    brief: Cash is for the run; Talent stays.
    body: Cash upgrades improve this run. Talent cards unlock after your first Prestige
      and remain through resets. Fame raises income; free draw credits and KK are
      separate balances.
  - id: talent-free
    title: Your free draws
    brief: Use a free credit without spending KK.
    body: "A 1\xD7 pull uses one free credit when available, otherwise 100 KK. A
      5\xD7 pull uses four free credits when available, otherwise 400 KK. Payments
      are never mixed. Results are saved before the animation; Continue reveals the
      same saved cards."
  - id: talent-duplicates
    title: Duplicates improve a card
    brief: The same card gains one level.
    body: A duplicate adds one level to that card and improves its effect. Rarity
      stays the same. Compare the exact effect before and after; your card levels
      survive Prestige.
  - id: second-gift
    title: Your second-Prestige gift
    brief: 100 Kaju Katli is yours to keep.
    body: The second Prestige grants 100 KK once. A KK draw costs 100; free draws
      use separate credits. You can keep the gift for later. Opening this page never
      spends it.
  - id: return-play
    title: Welcome back
    brief: Your offline cash is already saved.
    body: The amount shown was settled once from your departure sales rate, offline
      efficiency and time cap. Continue keeps it; reopening this screen does not
      grant it again. Resume product purchases or check Player for your next upgrades.
  heading: {fileID: 1087554368}
  body: {fileID: 163232552}
